Description: avcodec/hevc/parser: defer access unit boundaries until the next VCL
 A prefix SEI in a nonzero layer can begin an access unit, while a PPS
 between pictures of the same access unit does not begin another one.
 Splitting immediately on layer-zero non-VCL NAL units gets both cases
 wrong and can separate dependent pictures from their base pictures.
 .
 Keep the first eligible non-VCL boundary until the next VCL NAL unit.
 Use the increasing picture layer order required by H.265 F.7.4.2.4.4
 to keep pictures together and recognize a new access unit when the
 layer ID does not increase. This does not add POC-based detection for
 access units that omit lower layers.
 .
 Retain buffered lookahead explicitly, since a deferred boundary can
 coincide with END_NOT_FOUND, and save its timestamp before the input
 timestamp history expires. Bound lookahead to the parser API's offset
 range. Keep the existing layer-zero EOS/EOB splitting behavior.
 .
